%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: SubtitlesTable_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e0d730566caf14b4fb9298c4121a9d74, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 6742177569951744
    m_Localized: ...It was a map.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6742172834582528
    m_Localized: These places still remember... and the manuscript wasn't a myth.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6742149170319360
    m_Localized: ...But the Academy was wrong.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6742115204845568
    m_Localized: And that the manuscript was just a myth.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6742080794775552
    m_Localized: Nawar here... For years as an archaeologist, I was told these places
      were nothing but dead ruins...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6742053976395776
    m_Localized: Audio log... Day Three.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 724982419456
    m_Localized: Who... awakened the seal?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 744246857728
    m_Localized: ...Who are you?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 767114203136
    m_Localized: They call me... Wahaj.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 786496081920
    m_Localized: ...Guardian of the Mirror.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 805114597376
    m_Localized: ...I see it has chosen you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 827671564288
    m_Localized: One of the gates has awakened... let's go.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9435209650176
    m_Localized: ' '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7688499558993920
    m_Localized: Written from bottom to top... 'By Nata'. It's as if he passed through
      here in a hurry, yet refused to leave without a trace.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7688884822593536
    m_Localized: Sabig bin Kharba... He clearly wanted his name remembered here.
      Even his name radiates power, like a warning to those who follow.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7689553726001152
    m_Localized: These words are more than just a prayer... The author was in real
      distress. He left a plea to the heavens here, hoping someone would listen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7690195274158080
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s heartbreaking how some emotions transcend time... Someone
      wrote this pleading to the heavens after Salim left. We don't know if he was
      a husband or a lover, but the sorrow is etched into every letter."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7690467144749056
    m_Localized: The drought here must have been brutal. When people beg their gods
      for rain, it means the land has reached its breaking point.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7690698187984896
    m_Localized: Contrary to what we might expect, the author didn't hide his personal
      desires. He carved them frankly into the stone to outlive him.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7690894959562752
    m_Localized: It seems the author abandoned nomadic life due to poverty. This
      inscription hints that some Thamudic people migrated to cities seeking a better
      life.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7691127919595520
    m_Localized: Another inscription documenting the exact same heartbreak... "Salim
      left". It seems her story was well-known, or perhaps she returned to carve
      her pain once more in a different place.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7691387874168832
    m_Localized: He was searching for luck that the passing of time couldn't shatter.
      Sometimes a short sentence is enough to reveal the heavy burden its author
      was carrying.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7691536629354496
    m_Localized: The inscription points to tombs built on a nearby hill. Perhaps
      the location was chosen deliberately so they would remain visible to the living.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7691845879582720
    m_Localized: To Wahab El'... A very brief inscription. Just a proof of existence
      for someone who wanted to tie his name to his gods, staying under their protection.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7692042076540928
    m_Localized: '''By Muqim''... This name was carved vertically here. Sometimes,
      all a person seeks is not to be forgotten.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7692306187669504
    m_Localized: This inscription is crucial... It tells us that the people of this
      land weren't just nomads; they practiced agriculture many centuries ago.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7692505362583552
    m_Localized: Not everything carved in stone is profound... It seems this inscription
      is just mocking a guy named Sharaf. Humans really haven't changed much.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7692696350216192
    m_Localized: '''Hajjaj'' is an ancient, well-known name. Perhaps he was named
      this because he was born during a pilgrimage season or a major religious event.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7692927041130496
    m_Localized: '''Greetings from Sad and Ali''... An inscription joining two brothers.
      What''s beautiful here is that their mother, ''Nima'', is mentioned with them;
      perhaps she held a high status or was dearly loved.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7693144008282112
    m_Localized: "'By Ra\u2019ab bin Jamam'... Just a name carved quietly. Who knows
      what kind of life this man lived before ending up as a silent memory on this
      wall."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7693346932903936
    m_Localized: Owning a purebred mare was a sign of status and wealth. It seems
      the author was incredibly proud of his possession.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7693554395762688
    m_Localized: '''Jaba bin Af''... A very brief inscription. Perhaps he didn''t
      have time to write more, or maybe his name alone was enough to be recognized
      by everyone.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7693780376473600
    m_Localized: '''A''a stood guard''... This isn''t just a souvenir. It seems someone
      was standing watch here, leaving this mark to document a long guard shift in
      this desolate place.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7694138188353536
    m_Localized: '''By Basil''... He chose a name that reflects his bravery, ensuring
      it remains etched in stone just as it was in the memories of those who knew
      him.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7694335995924480
    m_Localized: This inscription is different... It was written for a troubled brother.
      A simple prayer, but it reveals the depth of love between them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7694353498755072
    m_Localized: The author of this inscription didn't ask for wealth or glory...
      All he wanted was for his ordeal to end.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7761095872860160
    m_Localized: Read Inscription
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
